<section id="help" class="help" aria-label="How to print">
    <div class="help-top">
        <h2>How to print</h2>
        <button type="button" class="help-close" aria-label="Close help" title="Close" @ref="_close" @onclick="Close">×</button>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>In two colours</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Click <b>Download 3MF</b>.</li>
            <li>Double-click the file to open it in Bambu Studio.</li>
            <li>Base and Letters come in as two parts of one object. Choose a filament for each.</li>
            <li>Slice and print.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>Good to know</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>An STL has no colours. Use 3MF to keep the two parts.</li>
            <li>The colours on this page are for the preview only. The real ones are the filaments you pick.</li>
            <li>The grams shown assume solid PETG, so they are an upper limit.</li>
            <li>A cup marker appears upside down and mirrored, because it prints name side down with no supports. Do not flip it.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h3>Your data</h3>
        <p>Names, settings and uploaded fonts stay in this browser. Nothing is sent anywhere.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="credits">
        <h3>Credits</h3>
        <p>Fonts: Gan CLM (GNU GPL v2), Chewy (Apache 2.0), the others SIL Open Font License 1.1. <a href="https://github.com/eladgl-dot/3d-name-tag-generator/tree/main/assets/fonts/licences" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full licence texts</a></p>
        <p>Libraries: three.js (MIT), Clipper2 (Boost), LibTessDotNet (SGI Free Software License B), SixLabors.Fonts (Apache 2.0).</p>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Close { get; set; }

    ElementReference _close;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender) await _close.FocusAsync();
    }
}
